# Databricks notebook deployment paths

When wiring Databricks notebook tasks in `jobs/resource_templates/*.yaml` (or any
new DAB resource file) and when deploying notebooks to the workspace, mirror the
in-repo `jobs/` tree under this workspace root:

```
/Workspace/Users/aditya.mandiwal@databricks.com/deployed from cursor/
```

The space in `deployed from cursor` is intentional and supported by the
Databricks Workspace API and DABs `notebook_path` field — keep it literal, no
URL-encoding, no quoting beyond the YAML scalar.

## Path mapping

| Repo file | Workspace `notebook_path` |
|---|---|
| `jobs/notebooks/<name>.ipynb` | `/Workspace/Users/aditya.mandiwal@databricks.com/deployed from cursor/jobs/notebooks/<name>` |
| `jobs/ddls/<name>.ipynb`      | `/Workspace/Users/aditya.mandiwal@databricks.com/deployed from cursor/jobs/ddls/<name>` |

The trailing `.ipynb` is dropped in `notebook_path` (Databricks resolves the
extension itself).

## Examples

```yaml
# notebook source
- task_key: pool_spends
  notebook_task:
    notebook_path: /Workspace/Users/aditya.mandiwal@databricks.com/deployed from cursor/jobs/notebooks/pool_spends_app
    source: WORKSPACE

# DDL source
- task_key: create_pool_tables
  notebook_task:
    notebook_path: /Workspace/Users/aditya.mandiwal@databricks.com/deployed from cursor/jobs/ddls/dbspend360_total_pool_spends
    source: WORKSPACE
```

## Do not

- Do NOT use the legacy `DBSpend360-app-v2/` workspace folder. It has been
  retired; all new and migrated tasks must use the `deployed from cursor/`
  root above.
- Do NOT flatten the `jobs/notebooks/` or `jobs/ddls/` subpath under the
  workspace root — the repo tree must mirror so name collisions stay
  impossible.
